what's it like?

2218
01:25:56,385 --> 01:25:58,053
- Oh, what difference
does it make?

2219
01:25:58,053 --> 01:25:59,988
Poor little me, I'm not news.

2220
01:25:59,988 --> 01:26:01,858
- Just try telling
that to my editor.

2221
01:26:01,858 --> 01:26:04,193
- Well, it's really was
because of my darling,

2222
01:26:04,193 --> 01:26:05,628
darling boy.

2223
01:26:05,628 --> 01:26:07,397
I've come home to be
a real mother to him.

2224
01:26:07,397 --> 01:26:08,798
- [Servo] Yeah, that's
fine, can I take your

2225
01:26:08,798 --> 01:26:09,998
lunch order now?

2226
01:26:09,998 --> 01:26:11,467
- I must confess
I've neglected him.

2227
01:26:11,467 --> 01:26:15,505
But now, now the curtain rises
on the bright new horizon.

2228
01:26:15,505 --> 01:26:16,772
- [Servo] Horizon.

2229
01:26:16,772 --> 01:26:19,642
- A new and lovely life
for just the two of us.

2230
01:26:19,642 --> 01:26:23,378
I realize that above all
things, I'm a mother.

2231
01:26:23,378 --> 01:26:24,313
- [Crow] Check that.

2232
01:26:24,313 --> 01:26:25,615
- And you may quote me on that.

2233
01:26:25,615 --> 01:26:26,983
- Well thank you, Miss Leland.

2234
01:26:26,983 --> 01:26:29,585
- [Joel] Oh, what a dark
comment on our society.

2235
01:26:30,820 --> 01:26:32,755
- [Crow] We've secretly
taken his live son

2236
01:26:32,755 --> 01:26:34,157
and replaced him
with this dead one.

2237
01:26:34,157 --> 01:26:35,792
Let's watch.

2238
01:26:35,792 --> 01:26:37,727
- [Joel] See what
coffee houses can do?

2239
01:26:40,897 --> 01:26:43,700
- [Servo] So, uh, all this
happened because Johnny got

2240
01:26:43,700 --> 01:26:44,800
lost at the fair?

2241
01:26:48,672 --> 01:26:50,473
- [Joel] Well, I guess
I'll have to give this hat

2242
01:26:50,473 --> 01:26:52,075
back to Colonel Blake now.

2243
01:26:53,677 --> 01:26:56,178
- [Crow] Cream chip
beef, that sounds good.

2244
01:26:56,178 --> 01:26:58,180
Wonder if I have any
toast in the house.

2245
01:26:59,448 --> 01:27:00,683
- [Servo] The sad
side of beatniks,

2246
01:27:00,683 --> 01:27:02,085
beyond the bongos
and the goatees,

2247
01:27:02,085 --> 01:27:03,587
lays pain.

2248
01:27:04,987 --> 01:27:07,457
- Edward Platt will be
back in "Shaft In Africa."

2249
01:27:10,860 --> 01:27:13,128
(whirring)

2250
01:27:20,837 --> 01:27:22,238
Say Joel,

2251
01:27:22,238 --> 01:27:24,407
why hasn't that conductor
guy, Merit Stone,

2252
01:27:24,407 --> 01:27:25,240
been in more movies?

2253
01:27:25,240 --> 01:27:26,308
He's pretty good.

2254
01:27:26,308 --> 01:27:27,543
- Yeah.

2255
01:27:27,543 --> 01:27:29,345
- (French accent) Ah ha,
so I see you too have

2256
01:27:29,345 --> 01:27:31,047
fallen into the trap.

2257
01:27:31,047 --> 01:27:33,315
- Right, why are you
dressed like Raleigh Fingers

2258
01:27:33,315 --> 01:27:34,750
at a Playboy party?

2259
01:27:34,750 --> 01:27:35,918
- Aw, what do you mean by that?

2260
01:27:35,918 --> 01:27:37,187
- Crow I'm not sure
but I think he's

2261
01:27:37,187 --> 01:27:38,755
playing the role
of Hercule Poirot,

2262
01:27:38,755 --> 01:27:40,290
the great detective.

2263
01:27:40,290 --> 01:27:41,590
- (French accent)
That is right Joel,

2264
01:27:41,590 --> 01:27:43,358
I suppose you are
all wondering--

2265
01:27:43,358 --> 01:27:44,927
- Wondering why I have
gathered you here today.

2266
01:27:44,927 --> 01:27:47,563
- Don't you ever step on
my line again, please.

2267
01:27:47,563 --> 01:27:50,433
I am here to solve the
great Merit Stone mystery.

2268
01:27:50,433 --> 01:27:52,702
- Uh, that's great, Tom,
but we've got a letter

2269
01:27:52,702 --> 01:27:53,535
here to read.

2270
01:27:53,535 --> 01:27:54,470
It comes from a Pat--

2271
01:27:54,470 --> 01:27:56,572
- Oh come on guys, please?

2272
01:27:56,572 --> 01:28:00,443
- Okay, Tom, what is the
great Merit Stone mystery?

2273
01:28:00,443 --> 01:28:03,078
- Thank you, Joel, now if
you will grab the visual aid

2274
01:28:03,078 --> 01:28:05,047
I have prepared and follow
along with me, please?

2275
01:28:05,047 --> 01:28:05,982
- Okay, got it.

2276
01:28:05,982 --> 01:28:07,917
- No one is to leave the room.

2277
01:28:07,917 --> 01:28:12,122
Now then, we all agree
that the Gary Busey like

2278
01:28:12,122 --> 01:28:15,725
conductor from "The Rebel
Set" is Merit Stone, right?

2279
01:28:15,725 --> 01:28:16,558
- Right.

2280
01:28:16,558 --> 01:28:17,993
- Wrong!

2281
01:28:17,993 --> 01:28:19,228
How could you be so
stupid, you make me puke!

2282
01:28:19,228 --> 01:28:22,698
- Geez, calm down, it's
just Merit Stone, Tom.

2283
01:28:22,698 --> 01:28:25,668
- And what is it that led you
pig dogs to the conclusion

2284
01:28:25,668 --> 01:28:27,570
that it was Merit Stone?

2285
01:28:27,570 --> 01:28:28,403
Gypsy!?

2286
01:28:29,838 --> 01:28:32,708
- 'Cause he was in "Earth vs.
Spider" and "The Tormented?"

2287
01:28:32,708 --> 01:28:34,343
- Wrong!

2288
01:28:34,343 --> 01:28:37,213
I too almost fell for
that foolish trap.

2289
01:28:37,213 --> 01:28:40,750
Joel, Merit Stone's name
appears in the credits to

2290
01:28:40,750 --> 01:28:44,353
"Earth vs. The Spider," "The
Magic Sword," and "Tormented."

2291
01:28:44,353 --> 01:28:45,422
Put them on the board please.

2292
01:28:45,422 --> 01:28:46,255
- Okay, got it.

2293
01:28:46,255 --> 01:28:47,657
- Thank you.

2294
01:28:47,657 --> 01:28:49,492
But, the Gary Busey conductor
guy physically appears

2295
01:28:49,492 --> 01:28:52,495
in "Earth Vs. Spider,"
"Rebel Set," "Giant Leeches,"

2296
01:28:52,495 --> 01:28:53,863
and "The Tormented."

2297
01:28:53,863 --> 01:28:56,232
Something was wrong.

2298
01:28:56,232 --> 01:28:57,300
They didn't match.

2299
01:28:57,300 --> 01:28:59,202
I put my gray matter together

2300
01:28:59,202 --> 01:29:02,372
and I realized that
Jack Kosslyn appears in

2301
01:29:02,372 --> 01:29:04,773
"The Magic Sword," and
"The Earth Vs. The Spider."

2302
01:29:04,773 --> 01:29:06,275
- You have a lot of
free time, don't you?

2303
01:29:06,275 --> 01:29:07,143
- Quiet fool!

2304
01:29:08,677 --> 01:29:12,548
Was it possible that
Jack Kosslyn was
actually Merit Stone?

2305
01:29:12,548 --> 01:29:13,917
And vice versa?

2306
01:29:14,783 --> 01:29:15,585
- Yes?

2307
01:29:15,585 --> 01:29:16,418
- No!

2308
01:29:16,418 --> 01:29:17,620
- Uh, no?

2309
01:29:17,620 --> 01:29:19,555
- Yes!

2310
01:29:19,555 --> 01:29:21,390
His name did not appear
in "The Rebel Set,"

2311
01:29:21,390 --> 01:29:23,760
"The Giant Leeches,"
or "Tormented."

2312
01:29:23,760 --> 01:29:24,993
I was back at the beginning.

2313
01:29:24,993 --> 01:29:27,630
Then a major break in the case.

2314
01:29:27,630 --> 01:29:30,165
Gene Roth's name appears
in the credits of

2315
01:29:30,165 --> 01:29:32,835
"Earth Vs. Spider," "Rebel
Set," "Giant Leeches,"

2316
01:29:32,835 --> 01:29:34,470
and "The Tormented."

2317
01:29:34,470 --> 01:29:35,303
(laughs)

2318
01:29:35,303 --> 01:29:36,972
I had my man.

2319
01:29:36,972 --> 01:29:40,375
Gentlemen, I put it
to you that Gene Roth

2320
01:29:40,375 --> 01:29:42,612
is actually Merit Stone.

2321
01:29:42,612 --> 01:29:44,347
- I'm so relieved.

2322
01:29:44,347 --> 01:29:45,582
- I plan to celebrate
with a bottle of

2323
01:29:45,582 --> 01:29:47,850
Chateau Marmont '52, and
perhaps a bit of brie.

2324
01:29:47,850 --> 01:29:50,318
- Whoa, whoa,
whoa, wait up here,

2325
01:29:50,318 --> 01:29:52,188
if Gene Roth is Merit Stone,

2326
01:29:52,188 --> 01:29:57,058
and Merit Stone is in "The
Magic Sword," with Jack Kosslyn,

2327
01:29:57,058 --> 01:29:59,295
couldn't Jack Kosslyn
actually be Merit Stone?

2328
01:29:59,295 --> 01:30:01,497
And transitively, Jack
Kosslyn could be Gene Roth.

2329
01:30:01,497 --> 01:30:02,798
- No, no, no, no, you silly man,

2330
01:30:02,798 --> 01:30:05,535
'cause we have a visual
idea of Merit, I mean--

2331
01:30:05,535 --> 01:30:07,937
- But you don't have a
visual idea of Jack Kosslyn.

2332
01:30:07,937 --> 01:30:09,572
- Not as such, but.

2333
01:30:09,572 --> 01:30:12,242
- Well then Jack Kosslyn
could be Merit Stone.

2334
01:30:13,642 --> 01:30:15,712
- And if Jack Kosslyn is
Merit Stone, and Merit Stone

2335
01:30:15,712 --> 01:30:17,813
is in "Tormented"
with Gene Roth,

2336
01:30:17,813 --> 01:30:20,182
then who is Jack Kosslyn
and couldn't Jack Kosslyn

2337
01:30:20,182 --> 01:30:21,550
be Gene Roth?

2338
01:30:21,550 --> 01:30:22,985
(stuttering)

2339
01:30:22,985 --> 01:30:24,187
(surge)

2340
01:30:24,187 --> 01:30:25,020
- Oh.

2341
01:30:26,188 --> 01:30:27,857
We gotta stop doing
that to that poor kid.

2342
01:30:27,857 --> 01:30:29,058
What do you think, sirs?

2343
01:30:29,992 --> 01:30:32,295
- Gene Roth.

2344
01:30:32,295 --> 01:30:35,465
Gene Roth was in "She Demons."

2345
01:30:35,465 --> 01:30:38,802
The 1958 film with
Irish McCallahan.

2346
01:30:40,637 --> 01:30:41,570
But Jack Kosslyn,

2347
01:30:42,738 --> 01:30:45,173
Jack Kosslyn wasn't
in "She Demons!"

2348
01:30:45,173 --> 01:30:46,142
(crying)

2349
01:30:46,142 --> 01:30:48,310
So who is Merit Stone?

2350
01:30:48,310 --> 01:30:50,980
Dear God, who is Merit Stone?

2351
01:30:50,980 --> 01:30:52,582
- I'll get you for this, Joel.

2352
01:30:53,482 --> 01:30:55,885
- [Frank] Who is Merit Stone!?

2353
01:31:01,890 --> 01:31:04,660
(reverent music)

2354
01:32:04,053 --> 01:32:05,220
- I am bugged.

